Figure 4 illustrates the active transport and distribution of Nano-11 nanoparticles within the draining lymph nodes post-injection. Flow cytometry plots (A) show Nano-11-containing myeloid cells peaking on day 2, with the percentage of these cells among all myeloid cells significantly higher on day 2 compared to days 1 and 7 (B). Migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) comprise the largest fraction (60–80%) of Nano-11-positive cells (C) and demonstrate the highest per-cell uptake of Nano-11, indicated by significantly greater mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs and monocytes/macrophages (D). This suggests Nano-11 effectively targets and is taken up by MigDCs, facilitating antigen delivery to the lymph nodes.